    }), "\n", _jsxs(_components.p, {
      children: [_jsx(_components.strong, {
        children: "Parallel stage execution"
      }), " optimizes latency in workflows where stages are independent. When generating a report with multiple sections, after the outline stage completes, all section generations can execute in parallel since they don't depend on each other's outputs. This parallelization dramatically reduces end-to-end latency-if each of five sections takes 30 seconds to generate, sequential execution requires 150 seconds while parallel execution completes in approximately 30 seconds. Implementation requires careful state management to collect parallel results and handle partial failures, but the latency improvements justify the complexity for high-throughput systems."]
    }), "\n", _jsxs(_components.p, {
